<title>POLAND: Poland raises 10-yr bond minimum price to 98.90.</title>
<headline>Poland raises 10-yr bond minimum price to 98.90.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland sold 1.5 million zlotys worth of ten-year floating bonds after investors bid for 127 million against the Treasury's 600 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The minimum price of the bonds, due April 18, 2007 rose to 98.90 from 98.51 at the last auction on January 14, 1997.</p>
<p>The average price was also 98.90, up from 98.60.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
